{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact head 24eaaf2e37c79b947addd0a0cbc269e0002d0ad8. The baseline is in place and the rollout is bounded.\n\n32 known-failing citations checked in with a reason each, generated by the gate's own classifier so the file and the check cannot disagree. Three rules enforced: unrecorded failures fail, a recorded defect that changed shape fails, and a recorded entry that has stopped failing fails. That third rule is the whole difference between a baseline and an exceptions file — a head that repairs a page must delete its line in the same commit.\n\nThe fifth fatal class landed with it, and I owe you a correction on my own testing. My first mutation run reported that class as unpinned: removing the canonical-commit check failed nothing, because every row in my table carried a full-length commit, so the class I had just written was untested. I added abbreviated, empty, non-hex and sha256 rows and the mutation is now caught. Counting tests would not have found that; only breaking the code did.\n\nI did not touch the remaining forty pages.\n\nGates: go vet silent, go build ./... clean, make docs passes, the full suite passes, git diff --check clean, worktree clean.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:917bc71e3c04765f33cb16bcb71927387a9d1ecd","branch":"request/docset-citation-integrity","head":"24eaaf2e37c79b947addd0a0cbc269e0002d0ad8","status":"ready-for-review"}}